PyTorch 2.11.0 for DeltaAI (CUDA 13.0, Python 3.12)
Includes: transformers, accelerate, datasets, peft, lightning,
          timm, bitsandbytes, diffusers, mpi4py, tensorboard,
          wandb, jupyter, scipy, scikit-learn, opencv, nvitop
New in this build (sm_90 source builds):
  flash-attn, transformer_engine, xformers, apex, mamba-ssm,
  triton, torch-geometric, cupy-cuda13x, tensorrt, flashinfer
Known: transformer_engine and cupy currently fail at import due to
  a cu13 libcublasLt / cython ABI mismatch on this stack — use the
  other attention paths (flash-attn, xformers) and stock torch CUDA
  until an upstream fix lands.

For documentation and examples:
  https://docs.ncsa.illinois.edu/systems/deltaai/

Run setup-kernel prior to launching OOD job.

Quick start (on a compute node):
  module load python/miniforge3_pytorch/2.11.0
  conda activate base
  python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())"

CUDA extensions: CUDA_HOME, nvcc, and CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH come from the
auto-loaded cuda/13.1.1 module.

